    {
      "evidence_id": "evidence-loop-unroll-prediction-gains--a4f79b2e6c18",
      "title": "Loop Unroll Prediction Gains",
      "excerpt": "They used over 2,500 loops from 72 benchmarks to train two machine learning models (a nearest neighbor and a support vector machines model) to predict the loop unroll factor for unseen loops. Using a richer set of features than [14], their techniques correctly predict the unroll factor for 65% of the testing loops, leading to on average, a 5% improvement for the SPEC 2000 benchmark suite.",
      "overview": "The loop-unrolling result is a quantitative benchmark for direct prediction. It does not prove that all compiler choices are easy to learn, but it demonstrates that for a bounded option set, feature-based supervised models can predict useful decisions and produce measurable application-level performance improvements.",
      "evidence_type": "statistical_result",
